{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the H1 follow-up: the single celld version pin, the wider smoke paths and the Lending version binding. The head is 48ce36ac524b3dcd0a28155e036b5a1357010b43 (tree c2f8d9811cdfe6cd4e478227c252fde5505e6f98), for request 5977cd77, under builder promise ee5a631e. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI read the implementation note a03b9107 first, then the request and every change from Main a78e0981.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. The head descends from Main a78e0981 through 3 commits. They change exactly the 8 paths named by the 8 artifacts, one artifact per path. None of the artifacts has been superseded, and all 8 are listed `current`. The worktree was clean at the head.\n- Checkpoint. 7b96bcb5 has tree c4ea31a4, as stated. From 7b96bcb5 to d90a023a, only the note and its manifest are added. From d90a023a to the head, only the note's provenance paragraph changes.\n- Fresh checks at 7b96bcb5. Each receipt records exit 0, and in each the source before and after is identical. Each output digest matches the note.\n  - Owning Node run: 8 tests, 8 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.\n  - Proxy run:\n    - configured create 201;\n    - unset, forwarded-only and wrong-service creates 403;\n    - a different Host accepted;\n    - two MCP sessions with two room tool calls;\n    - rotation 200 and retirement 200;\n    - 7 scopes verified;\n    - health 200;\n    - both celld processes exited 0 with no signal.\n  - Gate: exit 0, and the output ends \"gate passed\". Results:\n    - Node 76 passed;\n    - counting 55 passed;\n    - plain 2892 passed and 1 skipped;\n    - Native 822 passed and 2 skipped.\n- Evidence:\n  - The committed manifest has SHA-256 db0cc197…. All 57 entries match their recorded size and hash, and no entry is writable.\n  - SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 60641d61…, and all its 56 lines are OK.\n  - The original report tail's SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 0dc47fbe…. It holds 34 files, and all 33 lines are OK.\n  - The re-anchored report tail's SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 57cb65a8…. It holds 31 files, and all 30 lines are OK.\n  - No file in either tail is writable. Each digest is the one named in the reporting artifact.\n- Documents:\n  - check-doc-links on an export of the head: 725 links, 0 broken.\n  - check-notes a78e0981..48ce36ac: 0 warnings.\n  - check-commit-messages: 3 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - `git diff --check`: clean.\n\nI reran no suite and no proxy.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe head does the three items the request names, and nothing else.\n\n1. Single pin. `celldVersionOf` accepts exactly `v\u003cmajor\u003e.\u003cminor\u003e.\u003cpatch\u003e` followed by one newline, and refuses anything else. `matchesCelldVersion` compares whole whitespace-separated tokens of the binary's output with the pin, with or without the `v`. The driver now reads the pin only from apps/room/celld/celld.version, and both former `v0.6.2` literals are gone. The module runs its driver only when invoked directly, so the test can import the matcher. The workflow already read the same file and checks the same form. The test uses the real pin and a synthetic second pin, and covers neighbouring versions, prefixes, suffixes, a release-candidate suffix and nine malformed pin texts.\n2. Path filter. Both triggers add packages/cli, packages/platform, packages/derive and packages/bytes, and keep package.json and package-lock.json. The test parses each trigger block separately. Removing a path from one trigger fails that trigger's check and leaves the other passing. The action pins, permissions, branch restriction and steps are unchanged.\n3. Lending binding. apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc gains the same `version_metadata` line as the Grow, Demo and register configurations. health.ts already reads it, and it accepts only a UUID. docs/security/settings.md explains the binding in a new paragraph. The inventory row already listed `dap-lending` at Main, and with this head it is true.\n\nMerge plan. The builder says that stale predecessors are eligible. I read internal/mergeplan/mergeplan.go in ~/play/gitseq, and it agrees: `StandingArtifact` and `StandingStatement` refuse retired or ineffective events, and staleness alone does not withdraw them. The unit test includes a stale live artifact. Five of the eight paths have stale predecessors at a78e0981. I have not run a merge plan, and I have not confirmed that the installed `gs` matches that source. The builder's preview before the landing will show it.\n\n## Security\n\n- No runtime authority changes: no production TypeScript, native definition, pin, migration, dependency or secret.\n- The version binding is nonsecret, and Cloudflare Workers supplies its value. Health exposes only a validated version id, or `unknown`.\n- The driver is now stricter. A malformed pin file fails before any process starts. A prefix or suffix of the version is no longer enough for a binary to match.\n- The workflow keeps `contents: read`, no secrets, commit-pinned actions and attestation verification before decompression.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe production change is one configuration line. The driver change is 12 lines and removes two literals. The new tests (53 lines) are proportionate for a pin and a trigger list that would otherwise fail silently.\n\nOne point, not blocking. docs/celld.md line 48 still links to the celld documentation at the `v0.6.2` tag. A version bump would leave that link at the old release's documentation. The driver and the workflow read only celld.version, so the request's condition is met.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved. No authority changes. The pin check is stricter, and the new binding is nonsecret.\n- Simplification: approved, with the documentation link noted.\n- Request conditions:\n  - one head;\n  - owning checks for each item;\n  - ordinary gate passed at 7b96bcb5;\n  - note with sealed evidence;\n  - after the demo retirement (a78e0981), before 7ee9a63b.\n\nThis approval covers the software head 